<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  shiroikuma-nekokan fork: every string the fork adds (the launcher label sk_app_name excepted,
  which stays beside app_name in strings.xml).

  They live in a file of their own so that upstream's strings.xml stays as upstream wrote it,
  apart from the rebranded lines. Every string here that is not marked untranslatable has its
  Japanese translation in values-ja/sk_strings.xml, made in the same change — compare the two
  key sets before a build is called done. The other 53 locales fall back to English, hence the
  lint exemption.

  Among them: the `contains` list SkAutomationProvider.describe() hands a caller before any
  export exists (sk_eim_contains_*). 応用管理 renders these verbatim next to a "back this app up"
  row, so they say what the archive actually is: not a settings dump, but the barcodes of
  白い熊's loyalty and membership cards.
-->
